---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import QuickFacts from "../../components/QuickFacts.astro";
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

const primaryCta = site.phoneNumber && site.phoneNumber !== "PHONE_NUMBER"
  ? { href: `tel:${site.phoneNumber}`, text: `📞 ${site.phoneNumber}` }
  : { href: "/contact/", text: "📞 Call for a Free Consultation" };

const signs = [
  { name: "Salt Bridge", detail: "A hardened crust forms above the water level in the brine tank, so salt fails to dissolve into the water even though the tank looks full." },
  { name: "Salt Mush", detail: "Salt dissolves into a thick sludge at the bottom of the tank instead of a clean brine solution, blocking the float valve and intake screen." },
  { name: "Standing Water", detail: "Brine water that fails to drain down during regeneration usually points to a clogged injector or a stuck float valve." },
  { name: "Hard Water Despite Regeneration", detail: "If the tank isn't producing usable brine, the resin bed never gets properly recharged, and water tests hard even on schedule." },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: "How often does a water softener brine tank need cleaning?", a: "Salt refill and service interval for the equipment actually installed is [PLACEHOLDER — confirm maintenance frequency], more often in areas with high hardness or high iron content." },
  { q: "Can I clean my own brine tank?", a: "Yes, for routine cleaning — drain it, remove leftover salt, scrub with soap and water, and rinse thoroughly. A hardened salt bridge or a stuck float valve often needs a professional diagnostic." },
  { q: "What causes a salt bridge?", a: "High humidity, using the wrong salt type, or overfilling the tank all encourage salt to fuse into a solid crust above the water line." },
  { q: "Does a dirty brine tank damage the softener?", a: "Yes — over time it affects the resin bed's ability to fully regenerate, shortening the resin's effective lifespan and reducing softening performance." },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`Brine Tank Cleaning in ${site.city}, ${site.stateAbbr}`}
  description={`Signs your ${site.city} water softener's brine tank needs cleaning, what it involves, and how the process works.`}
>
  <PageHero
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Repair", href: "/repair/" }, { label: "Brine Tank Cleaning" }]}
    heading={`Brine Tank Cleaning in ${site.city}, ${site.stateAbbr} | Trusted Local Specialists`}
    primaryCta={primaryCta}
    secondaryCta={{ href: "/quote/", text: "Get a Free Water Softener Quote in Albuquerque" }}
  >
    <p slot="opening">
      <a href="/" class="brand-link">Water Softeners of {site.city}</a>
      {" "}offers brine tank cleaning services across {site.city} and {site.county} at {site.gpgLow}
      –{site.gpgHigh} GPG from {site.waterAuthority}, such as salt bridge removal and float valve inspection.
      Salt refill and service interval for the equipment actually installed is [PLACEHOLDER — confirm
      maintenance frequency]. Salt bridges, salt mushing, and dirty brine reduce regeneration effectiveness and
      waste salt. Free diagnostic included with every cleaning call. Same day availability.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <QuickFacts />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p>The brine tank holds the salt solution a water softener uses to regenerate its resin bed. At {site.gpgLow}-{site.gpgHigh} GPG, {site.city} softeners, such as single-tank and combo systems, regenerate more often than in a moderate-hardness market, which means more salt cycling through the tank and a shorter interval before it needs attention.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Signs Your Brine Tank Needs Cleaning</h2>
      <p>Four symptoms point specifically to a brine tank issue, not a resin bed or control head fault. These signs cover the most common causes:</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        {signs.map((s) => (
          <div class="card">
            <p class="card-title">{s.name}</p>
            <p>{s.detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Brine Tank Cleaning Cost</h2>
        <p>Actual price range for this service is [PLACEHOLDER — confirm local price range for brine tank cleaning]. Clearing a hardened salt bridge or replacing a stuck float valve costs more, depending on what's found during diagnosis — get a free diagnostic to confirm yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center">
        <h2>How Brine Tank Cleaning Works</h2>
        <p>Three steps restore usable brine, each building on the last.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="process-number">1</span>
          <p class="card-title">Drain and Empty</p>
          <p>We bypass the softener, drain remaining brine, and remove any leftover salt, sludge, or a hardened bridge.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="process-number">2</span>
          <p class="card-title">Clean and Inspect</p>
          <p>We scrub the tank with soap and water, then inspect the float valve, injector, and grid plate for buildup or damage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="process-number">3</span>
          <p class="card-title">Refill and Test</p>
          <p>We refill with fresh salt, run a manual regeneration cycle, and confirm the system is producing usable brine again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Connection to Resin Bed Performance</h2>
        <p>A dirty brine tank starves the resin bed of the concentrated brine it needs to fully regenerate. Compared to resin bed replacement, brine tank cleaning is the simpler, lower-cost fix, and it is always worth ruling out first. If the resin itself has already failed, see our <a href="/resin-bed-replacement/">Water Softener Resin Bed Replacement in Albuquerque</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center">
        <h2>Brine Tank Cleaning Questions</h2>
        <p>{site.waterAuthority} reports the {site.gpgLow}-{site.gpgHigh} GPG figure behind every answer below.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              {item.q}
              <svg class="faq-chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 6.5 8 10.5 12 6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container final-cta">
      <h2>Brine Tank Acting Up in {site.city}?</h2>
      <p>Free in-home diagnostic to confirm whether the brine tank is the cause.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote/">Get a Free Water Softener Quote in Albuquerque</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .process-step { text-align: center; padding: 0 12px; }
    .process-number {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 40px;
      height: 40px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-full, 9999px);
      background: var(--color-primary-light);
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }
    .card-title { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--surface-footer); margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .faq-list { max-width: 760px; margin: 24px auto 0; }
    .final-cta { text-align: center; }
    .final-cta p { max-width: 48ch; margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
